{#- The plain index pagehead: a kicker, a title, an optional standfirst, the
    rule. Every index that is just a title over a list uses this; a page
    whose header carries more than that — actions, a mark, a byline — writes
    its own, since forcing those into one more parameter each would make
    this harder to read than the markup it replaces. sub is trusted markup
    rather than escaped text, since the search index's standfirst carries a
    <kbd>; a caller with nothing to mark up still passes plain text through
    unharmed. -#}
{% macro simple(title, kicker="Index", sub="") %}
<header class="pagehead">
  <p class="pagehead__kicker">{{ kicker }}</p>
  <h1 class="pagehead__title">{{ title }}</h1>
  {%- if sub %}<p class="pagehead__sub">{{ sub | safe }}</p>{% endif %}
  <hr class="pagehead__rule">
</header>
{% endmacro %}
